window.docContents[24].resolve({"/Evidence-and-selected-direct-proof-calls/#Fluctuations-of-Riesz-gases--Evidence-and-selected-direct-proof-calls--Seven-selected-proof-calls":{"contents":"The following seven direct calls connect the commutator and Gaussian-comparison arguments. The linked proofs give their other dependencies.\n\n* HRS.screening_comparison_proof calls HRS.Main.A8P.a8p_commSpec to obtain the commutator constants and specification. Source, line 52.* HRS.screening_comparison_proof calls HRS.scrn_instance for scales at most one. The larger-scale case is handled separately. Source, line 53.* HRS.screening_stationary_limit_proof calls HRS.screening_error_tendsto for the five error terms, with the particle count shifted by two. Temperature mismatch is handled separately. Source, line 150.* HRS.screening_stationary_limit_proof calls HRS.scrn_stat_gauss_tendsto to pass from the transient Gaussian to the stationary Gaussian for fixed tests and lags. Source, line 155.* HRS.Commutator.TorusNote.commutator_estimate_sub_of_torus calls HRS.Commutator.TorusNote.torus_subcoulomb_commutator, specializing the sharp result to a probability density. Source, line 83.* HRS.Commutator.TorusNote.commutator_estimate_sub_of_torus calls HRS.Commutator.TorusNote.embedding_T to supply the sharper theorem’s fractional transport bound from the application’s higher-derivative bound. Source, line 84.* HRS.Commutator.commutator_estimate_of_packets calls HRS.Commutator.TorusNote.commutator_estimate_sub_of_torus in its sub-Coulomb branch. The remaining branch is separate. Source, line 51.\n\n\n","context":"Fluctuations of Riesz gases\u0009Evidence and selected direct proof calls","header":"4.3. Seven selected proof calls","id":"/Evidence-and-selected-direct-proof-calls/#Fluctuations-of-Riesz-gases--Evidence-and-selected-direct-proof-calls--Seven-selected-proof-calls"}});